---
<SiteLayout title="Engine of World — Worldeology Lab" description="Engine of World studies persistent, causal, and consequential environments for interactive intelligence." headerTone="paper" active="research" image="/og.png">
  <main id="main" class="lab-site lab-page research-field-page program-world">
    <header class="research-field-header">
      <p class="lab-index"><a href="/research/">Research</a> / Engine of World</p>
      <h1>Engine of<br />World</h1>
      <p>Building persistent worlds in which intelligence can act, remember, and encounter consequences.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="research-proposition" aria-label="Engine of World proposition">
      <p class="program-lead">An interactive world is not a static scene. It is a causal system that continues after an action.</p>
      <p>Physical state is only one layer. A consequential world also contains beliefs, relationships, roles, institutions, durable memory, and unrealized future branches. These hidden states determine what an action means and which futures remain reachable.</p>
      <p class="program-thesis">Engine of World makes long-horizon consequence observable.</p>
      <p>We study environments that preserve latent state, generate causal event chains, and allow agents to act across extended horizons. The objective is not visual realism alone, but worlds coherent enough for counterfactual reasoning, social learning, and the evaluation of decisions whose effects emerge slowly.</p>
      <p>Such worlds become scientific instruments: places where intelligence can form plans, revise them, influence other agents, and bear the consequences of what it sets in motion.</p>
    </article>
    <section class="research-work-index" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <p id="work-title" class="lab-index">Selected work</p>
      <a href="/faculty/zhangxm/projects/mariolm/"><span>MarioLM</span><small>Persistent and consequential interactive worlds</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03999"><span>Long-Horizon Deception</span><small>Safety across extended interaction</small><i>↗</i></a>
    </section>
    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
